.TH GIT-PREFLIGHT 1
.SH NAME
git-preflight \- check Git repositories for local state before leaving a checkout behind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git preflight
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpath\fR]
.br
.B git-preflight
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpath\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-preflight
checks whether Git repositories contain local state that would be lost or stranded
if the checkout disappeared. It is intended as a workspace-level safety check,
not as a replacement for
.BR git-status (1).
.PP
By default, clean repositories produce no output. Any normal output means that
attention is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Recursively scan for Git repositories below the path. Nested repositories,
submodules, and worktrees are inspected independently.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print clean repositories as well as repositories with findings.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON. Clean repositories are included only with
.BR \-\-verbose .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress normal output. Exit codes still apply.
.TP
.BR \-\-fail-fast
Stop scanning after the first repository with local state.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-stash
Do not consider stash entries local state.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-operations
Do not consider in-progress Git operations local state.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH FINDINGS
Findings are printed in this order when present:
.BR dirty ,
.BR error ,
.BR staged ,
.BR detached ,
.BR noremote ,
.BR unpushed ,
.BR unstaged ,
.BR stash ,
and
.BR operation .
.PP
.B unstaged
includes untracked, non-ignored files. Ignored files do not count as local
state.
.SH OUTPUT
Human output is line-oriented:
.PP
.EX
unpushed unstaged  site
noremote           plugin
.EE
.PP
JSON output has this shape:
.PP
.EX
{
  "root": "/home/user/repos",
  "recursive": true,
  "repositories": [
    {"path": "/home/user/repos/site", "findings": ["unpushed", "unstaged"]}
  ]
}
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No local state found.
.TP
.B 1
Local state found.
.TP
.B 2
Operational error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
git preflight
git preflight -r ~/repos
git preflight -r --verbose --json ~/repos
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-status (1),
.BR git-rev-parse (1)
